Minato's patch to frameworks/base's media/java/android/media/MediaExtractor.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0),
ADR-0060 e2d part 2b: the static initializer loads no libmedia_jni, and a path takes no http service.

Why: as MediaCodec's (mediacodec-without-media-jni.patch), its natives are libandroid_runtime's
(framework/native/android_runtime/android_media_MediaExtractor.cpp), registered when the process starts. Minato has no
http service for media (MediaHTTPService and IMediaHTTPService are not taken), so a path goes to the natives without
one, as Android's does for a path that is not an http or https URL; an http or https URL then fails as Android's
DataSourceFactory fails without a service ("Invalid http service!"), with the IOException setDataSource throws for any
source that does not open (a named limit, ADR-0060 e2d).

--- a/media/java/android/media/MediaExtractor.java
+++ b/media/java/android/media/MediaExtractor.java
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@
         }
 
         nativeSetDataSource(
-                MediaHTTPService.createHttpServiceBinderIfNecessary(path),
+                null /* Minato: no http service, MediaHTTPService.createHttpServiceBinderIfNecessary(path) */,
                 path,
                 keys,
                 values);
@@ -200,7 +200,7 @@
      */
     public final void setDataSource(@NonNull String path) throws IOException {
         nativeSetDataSource(
-                MediaHTTPService.createHttpServiceBinderIfNecessary(path),
+                null /* Minato: no http service, MediaHTTPService.createHttpServiceBinderIfNecessary(path) */,
                 path,
                 null,
                 null);
@@ -803,7 +803,7 @@
     private native final void native_finalize();
 
     static {
-        System.loadLibrary("media_jni");
+        // Minato: the natives are libandroid_runtime's (android_media_MediaExtractor.cpp), registered at the start.
         native_init();
     }
 
